form.addEventListener('submit', event => {
  event.preventDefault();
  document.getElementById('sent').textContent = new URLSearchParams(new FormData(form)).toString();
  document.getElementById('return-shown').textContent = document.getElementById('return').value;
});
```

This takes the form data and converts it to a URLSearchParams string. The FormData API will use the current value of the input fields.

Therefore, the problem must be that the value of the departure date input (#departure) is being changed to a locale-specific string (like "10/22/2026") at some point during the interaction.

